`BIDSDataset` loads raw recordings saved as FIF under `eeg/`, such as preprocessing derivatives: every one of them failed with `File does not exist`. The loader looked for every file of a recording and dropped their extension, which MNE-BIDS fills back in only for the BIDS formats of the datatype, and FIF is none for EEG. It now looks only for the data files MNE-BIDS reads (a BrainVision recording is its `.vhdr`) and keeps their extension. As for saved epochs, a recording with two such files, as two `desc` versions, raises an error asking for `description` instead of loading one of them.
